ct only, specific taxa, treatment arms (with/without immunotherapy). Good for Ch2_Clinical and Ch4_Context (treatment context).\n\nP0435: Review of ICI resistance mechanisms - Full review, includes microbiome section with specific taxa and mechanisms (TLR4, IL-12, metabolites). Good for Ch3_Mechanisms and Ch6_Challenges.\n\nP0436: Mucosal melanoma microbiome study protocol - Abstract only, baseline data collection, no results yet. Limited use, maybe Ch6_Challenges for methodological considerations.\n\nP0437: Gene-level microbiome signatures across cancer types - Full text, gene-level vs taxonomy, treatment-specific (CICB vs monotherapy), age stratification. Excellent for Ch2_Clinical, Ch3_Mechanisms, Ch4_Context.\n\nP0438: GI cancer resistance and microbiota review - Full review, GI-specific, mechanisms (SCFAs, bile acids, immune cell training), specific bacteria. Good for Ch2_Clinical, Ch3_Mechanisms, Ch4_Context.\n\nP0439: Gut microbiome for CRC immunotherapy review - Full review, MSS/pMMR focus, specific taxa, mechanisms, interventions. Good for Ch2_Clinical, Ch3_Mechanisms, Ch5_Interventions, Ch6_Challenges.\n\nP0440: Observational study of ICI usage patterns - Full text, real-world efficacy/toxicity, NOT microbiome. Limited relevance, Ch4_Context for clinical baseline.\n\nP0441: ICI as chemotherapy sensitization - Abstract only, clinical outcomes, NOT microbiome. Limited relevance, Ch4_Context for treatment sequencing.\n\nP0442: Microbiome and gynaecological cancer - Abstract + snippets, includes FMT and specific strains for ICI. Good for Ch3_Mechanisms and Ch5_Interventions.\n\nP0443: NSCLC microbiome signatures by PFS and PD-L1 - Full text, species-level taxa (Alistipes, Streptococcus), machine learning, chemo pre-treatment effects. Excellent for Ch2_Clinical, Ch3_Mechanisms, Ch4_Context.\n\nP0444: Microbial metabolic pathways guide ICB response - Full text, functional pathways (MEP, riboflavin), specific T cells (Vδ2, MAIT). Excellent for Ch3_Mechanisms and 